Z||000000||Cozmo||08-17-2001||10:19 AM||||We're getting ready to install a new engine in my compatriot's newly acquired '86 black GT. (you would not believe how LOUD rod knock can be...)<BR>It is an auto, we have a donor car ('86 GT, 85K miles) that is a stick.<BR>From what I understand, between the two cars we have all the pieces needed to do the swap.<BR>Our plan is to pull both cradles and then swap engines. (She wants to keep it auto).  <BR>I assume we can just remove the flywheel on the donor engine and install the TC and flexplate from the original engine...<BR>Any "gotchas" or arcane info we should know before we tear into this?<BR>We start tomorrow, if anyone in the St. Pete area wants to shadow this, we'll have dogs and burgers on the grill and plenty of "racing fuel" (beer). Email me bcardone@ij.net or call 727-480-7365 if you want to join in on the fun.<BR>Get ready to welcome a new Fiero owner!!!<BR>Next is her "Pennocks moniker"...<BR>BobC   ||||reg||10
